# Drupal config YAML is machine-generated and exported by the config system;
# prettier's opinions about it are neither wanted nor stable.
#
# drupal.org's CI writes exactly this file when a project does not ship one, so
# committing it changes nothing there. It matters locally: ddev-drupal-contrib
# writes its copy at the repository root and then runs eslint from inside the
# module directory, where prettier cannot see it — so without this file the
# local run reports errors on every config file and disagrees with CI.
*.yml
